# Sprint: Semantic Product Matching with Console Logging

## Overview
**Goal**: Enable catalogue to return semantically matched products (products that match catalogue item name perfectly) per catalogue item, with matches logged in console.

**Current State**: 
- VFS architecture is complete and validated
- Products are fetched via `catalogueLocationKeys` array matching
- No semantic validation that products actually match the category meaning
- No console logging of semantic matches

**Target State**:
- Products returned for a catalogue item are semantically validated
- Semantic match scores are logged to console
- Mismatches (products in wrong categories) are flagged
- All existing functionality preserved (zero regression)

---

## Regression Risk Assessment

**Code Areas at Risk**:
1. `sanity/lib/products/getSelectedProducts.ts` - Core product query logic (HIGH RISK)
2. `data/catalogue.ts` - VFS resolution and validation functions (MEDIUM RISK)
3. `app/(store)/products/[...category]/page.tsx` - Category page data fetching (HIGH RISK)
4. `app/(store)/products/page.tsx` - All products page (MEDIUM RISK)
5. `sanity/schemaTypes/productType.ts` - Product schema (LOW RISK - additive only)

**Risk Mitigation Strategy**:
- All changes are additive (new functions, logging wrappers)
- Zero modifications to existing query logic
- Feature flag for semantic validation (can be disabled)
- Comprehensive regression tests before any changes

---

## Scope Contract 1: Semantic Validation Engine

**Objective**: Create a utility that scores how well a product matches a catalogue category semantically.

**Files to Create**:
- `lib/catalogue/semanticMatching.ts` - Core semantic matching logic
- `lib/catalogue/semanticConfig.ts` - Semantic category definitions

**DoD - Layer 1 (Structure)**:
- [ ] Function `analyzeSemanticMatch(product, categorySlug)` exists with proper TypeScript types
- [ ] Function returns structured result: `{ score: number, reasons: string[], concerns: string[] }`
- [ ] Semantic configuration object exists mapping category slugs to keyword rules
- [ ] All 22 leaf catalogue categories have semantic definitions

**DoD - Layer 2 (Layout)**:
- [ ] Score calculation algorithm implemented with weighted scoring
- [ ] Keyword matching is case-insensitive
- [ ] Positive and negative keyword support
- [ ] Score ranges from 0-100 with clear thresholds

**DoD - Layer 3 (Surface)**:
- [ ] Semantic categories match business domain (audio equipment)
- [ ] Keywords derived from real product data patterns
- [ ] Brand matching incorporated in scoring
- [ ] Edge cases handled (multiple categories, ambiguous products)

**DoD - Layer 4 (Interaction)**:
- [ ] Performance: Scoring completes in <1ms per product
- [ ] Memory efficient: No unnecessary object allocations
- [ ] Deterministic: Same input always produces same score

**Verification (Testing)**:
- [ ] Unit test: Open-back headphones match "open-back" category (score >= 80)
- [ ] Unit test: Closed-back headphones don't match "open-back" (score < 40)
- [ ] Unit test: DAC/Amp combo matches both "dac-amp-combos" and "desktop-amps" categories
- [ ] Unit test: Earpads match "earpads" category (score >= 80)
- [ ] Unit test: Random unrelated product scores < 20 for all categories
- [ ] Performance test: 1000 products scored in <100ms

---

## Scope Contract 2: Console Logging Integration

**Objective**: Add semantic match logging to the product fetch flow without disrupting existing functionality.

**Files to Modify**:
- `sanity/lib/products/getSelectedProducts.ts` - Add logging wrapper

**DoD - Layer 1 (Structure)**:
- [ ] New function `getSelectedProductsWithLogging()` wraps existing function
- [ ] Logging only occurs when `process.env.NODE_ENV !== 'production'` or explicit flag set
- [ ] Log format is structured and readable

**DoD - Layer 2 (Layout)**:
- [ ] Console output shows: Category name, product count, semantic match summary
- [ ] Per-product logging shows: Product name, category, match score, pass/fail status
- [ ] Summary statistics logged: Total products, valid matches, questionable matches, invalid matches

**DoD - Layer 3 (Surface)**:
- [ ] Log colors/emojis: ✅ for strong matches (score >= 80), ⚠️ for moderate (60-79), ❌ for weak (< 60)
- [ ] Category context included in logs (breadcrumbs)
- [ ] Timestamp and query duration included

**DoD - Layer 4 (Interaction)**:
- [ ] Logging is non-blocking (async fire-and-forget)
- [ ] Errors in logging don't affect product fetch
- [ ] Can be disabled via environment variable

**Verification (Testing)**:
- [ ] Regression test: Products still fetch correctly when logging enabled
- [ ] Regression test: Products still fetch correctly when logging disabled
- [ ] Manual verification: Console output is readable and informative
- [ ] Edge case: Empty category shows appropriate message
- [ ] Edge case: Category with 50+ products shows summary instead of individual logs

---

## Scope Contract 3: Category Page Integration

**Objective**: Integrate semantic validation into the category page without changing UX.

**Files to Modify**:
- `app/(store)/products/[...category]/page.tsx` - Add semantic validation call

**DoD - Layer 1 (Structure)**:
- [ ] Semantic validation runs after product fetch
- [ ] Validation results available in page component (for future UI use)
- [ ] Zero changes to component props or returned JSX

**DoD - Layer 2 (Layout)**:
- [ ] Console shows category-specific header: "=== Category: [Name] ==="
- [ ] Console shows resolved catalogue keys
- [ ] Console shows semantic match breakdown by product

**DoD - Layer 3 (Surface)**:
- [ ] Integration respects existing parallel data fetching pattern
- [ ] No waterfall requests introduced
- [ ] Server Component remains async/await clean

**DoD - Layer 4 (Interaction)**:
- [ ] No client-side JavaScript added
- [ ] No hydration mismatches
- [ ] Fast page load preserved

**Verification (Testing)**:
- [ ] E2E test: Navigate to /products/headphones/open-back - products load
- [ ] E2E test: Navigate to /products/audio-electronics/desktop-amps - products load
- [ ] E2E test: Navigate to /products/accessories/earpads - products load
- [ ] Regression test: All existing E2E tests pass
- [ ] Console verification: Semantic matches logged for each category

