## Sprint Execution Sequence

**Phase 1: Foundation (Day 1)**
1. Write regression tests first (Scope Contract 4)
2. Run tests - verify they fail as expected (no semantic code yet)
3. Create semantic configuration (Scope Contract 1, Layer 1)
4. Implement semantic scoring algorithm (Scope Contract 1, Layer 2)

**Phase 2: Core Implementation (Day 2)**
5. Complete semantic validation engine (Scope Contract 1, Layers 3-4)
6. Run unit tests - verify semantic matching works
7. Implement console logging (Scope Contract 2, Layers 1-2)
8. Add logging polish (Scope Contract 2, Layers 3-4)

**Phase 3: Integration (Day 3)**
9. Integrate into category page (Scope Contract 3)
10. Run regression tests - verify zero breakage
11. Run E2E tests - verify console logging appears
12. Performance test - verify no degradation

**Phase 4: Verification (Day 4)**
13. Manual testing on all 22 category pages
14. Verify semantic match quality
15. Final regression test run
16. Documentation update

---

## Success Criteria

**Functional**:
- [ ] Navigating to any category page logs semantic matches to console
- [ ] Products with score >= 80 show as ✅ VALID
- [ ] Products with score < 40 show as ❌ MISMATCH (flagged for review)
- [ ] All existing product fetch functionality works unchanged

**Performance**:
- [ ] Page load time increase < 50ms (semantic validation overhead)
- [ ] Console logging overhead < 10ms per page
- [ ] No memory leaks from logging

**Quality**:
- [ ] All regression tests pass
- [ ] All new unit tests pass
- [ ] All E2E tests pass
- [ ] No TypeScript errors
- [ ] No ESLint warnings

---

## Rollback Plan

If any critical issues arise:
1. Disable semantic logging via environment variable
2. Revert to `getSelectedProducts()` without wrapper
3. All existing functionality remains intact

---

